<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport"
          content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Color Theory</title>
</head>

<body>

<header>

    <h1>🎨 Color Theory</h1>

    <p>
        A simple guide to understanding colors.
    </p>

</header>

<hr>

<main>

<section>

    <h2>🔴 Primary Colors</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Red</li>
        <li>Blue</li>
        <li>Yellow</li>
    </ul>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>🟠 Secondary Colors</h2>

    <table border="1" cellpadding="10">

        <tr>
            <th>Color Combination</th>
            <th>Result</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Red + Yellow</td>
            <td>Orange</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Blue + Yellow</td>
            <td>Green</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Red + Blue</td>
            <td>Purple</td>
        </tr>

    </table>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>🌈 Color Categories</h2>

    <dl>

        <dt><strong>Warm Colors</strong></dt>
        <dd>Colors commonly associated with warmth and energy.</dd>

        <dt><strong>Cool Colors</strong></dt>
        <dd>Colors commonly associated with calmness and coolness.</dd>

        <dt><strong>Neutral Colors</strong></dt>
        <dd>Colors such as black, white and gray.</dd>

    </dl>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>💡 Design Tip</h2>

    <p>
        Good color combinations can improve readability
        and visual communication.
    </p>

</section>

</main>

<footer>

    <hr>

    <p>
        Color Theory — HTML Learning Project
    </p>

</footer>

</body>
</html>
